<title>SWEDEN: Perstorp four-month profit falls 35 pct.</title>
<headline>Perstorp four-month profit falls 35 pct.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Four months from September 1 to December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>					(million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Pre-tax profit			  149   vs    228</p>
<p> Operating income		    3,788   vs  3,559*</p>
<p> Operating profit</p>
<p> after depreciation		   186    vs    271</p>
<p> Operating costs		    3,427    vs  3,785</p>
<p> Depreciation			   175    vs    204</p>
<p> Net financial items     CHARGE    37    vs     43  CHARGE</p>
<p> Minorities		  CHARGE     8    vs	5  CHARGE</p>
<p>NOTE -- * This figure compares operations that the company had in both periods, Perstorp said in its results statement.</p>
<p>Otherwise the comparison figure for the first four month period in the 1995/96 financial year is 4.260 billion crowns, it said.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
</text>
